# .env.example - every environment variable the ChainAIM Deep Research Agent reads.
#
# HOW TO USE
#   1. Copy this file to .env in the same folder (repo root).
#   2. Fill in only the values you need for the features you use.
#   3. .env is git-ignored (see .gitignore). NEVER commit it and NEVER paste its
#      values into a chat, issue, PR or log.
#
# Nothing reads .env yet: loading is added together with the first feature that
# needs a key (PR-6, GitHub summaries). See DESIGN/07-build-plan.md.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 1 - PR-6 GitHub summaries (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Fine-grained personal access token, read-only ("Contents: read",
# "Metadata: read"). Without it: public repos only, 60 requests/hour.
# With it: private repos you can read, 5,000 requests/hour.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 2 - PR-7 scheduled (headless) runs on your Claude Max plan
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Created with:  claude setup-token
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 2 - PR-9 discovery
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# YouTube Data API v3 key (Google Cloud console). Search has a small daily
# quota; the pipeline stops before it is used up.
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
# Tavily web search / extract (free tier: 1,000 credits per month).
TAVILY_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model provider - READ BEFORE ADDING
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is deliberately NOT listed as a value here.
# In subscription mode (config.yaml model.provider: subscription) it must be
# UNSET, otherwise Claude Code silently bills the API instead of your Max plan;
# `uv run scripts/orchestrate.py --provider-check` fails loudly if it is set.
# Only set it (in your shell, not here) when model.provider is "api".
